  "text": "Introduces a condition: something that might happen.\n\nThe moving parts of the hand used to touch and hold.\n\nGo after something or understand how events connect.\n\nPip, Sol and Grandma are here. Mara remains at work.\n\nMakes a statement negative, or says there isn't any.\n\nMara and the boy mend the bird’s torn wing together.\n\nCloser to Pip’s starting bank in these instructions.\n\nA person travelling in a vehicle but not driving it.\n\nMara told The Torn Wing to the people in the garden.\n\nShort for let us; suggests doing something together.\n\nM0-57q-32-17-27-41 21 0 27 16 7-17 27-16 7 24-27 41Z\n\nRelease an attachment before adjusting this section.\n\nAfter the last boat returns · Pip reads Mara’s story\n\nA flat surface where food can be prepared or served.\n\nStrong cords used here to hold the bridge in place.\n\nShows who something is meant for or why it is done.\n\nPut things together into a container to carry them.\n\nHere, not working very well as the thing described.\n\nSol has arrived. Mara is still working at the dock.\n\nSomething used in place of an old or damaged thing.\n\nHeld and moved something from one place to another.\n\nPut something down carefully in a particular place.\n\nAn expression of pleasure that someone has arrived.\n\nReach Grandma’s garden and plant the seed together.\n\nStayed until something happened or someone arrived.\n\nThe part of the body between the shoulder and hand.\n\nRehearsing Sol’s ending · Pip waits at the workshop\n\nThin material used for writing, drawing or folding.\n\nGrandma wants to thank Mara for staying to listen.\n\nThe foods or materials combined to make something.\n\nM19 166q23 7 45 0m23 15q26 7 44 0m-83-41q20 6 37 0\n\nAfter the last boat returns · Mara tells her story\n\nCarry the copy back across the footbridge to Mara.",
